    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I see. So it's the physics of the bore and the reed creating that specific harmonic profile. If we're looking at the flute again, are there any specific frequencies or \"unwanted\" nonlinearities that can disrupt that purer sound? I've heard people talk about certain \"ghostly\" qualities or artifacts in specialized recordings—is there a mathematical explanation for when those extra, unpredictable overtones show up?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
