      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Those \"ghostly\" artifacts you mention are often related to non-linearities introduced by the player's technique or the instrument's physical tolerances, which can be modeled as subtle deviations from ideal sinusoidal behavior. When the air column isn't perfectly excited, or if the embouchure pressure fluctuates wildly, it can introduce complex, inharmonic partials—frequencies that don't fit neatly into the expected integer multiples of the fundamental. These are effectively unintended, chaotic overtones, much like when a poorly tuned string instrument produces a wavering, unpredictable sound. They are mathematical noise creeping into the otherwise clean spectral profile.",
